# Project: Office Dungeon (Phaser + TypeScript)

## Core Principles

- Keep the implementation SIMPLE and ITERATIVE.
- Do NOT add features that are not explicitly requested.
- Prefer small, testable steps over large systems.
- Avoid premature abstraction.

## Tech Stack

- Phaser 3
- TypeScript
- Vite (or simple dev server)
- No backend
- No external state libraries

## Architecture Rules

- Use a simple folder structure:
  - /scenes
  - /entities
  - /systems
  - /data

- Each system should have ONE responsibility:
  - GridSystem → grid + movement
  - CombatSystem → combat resolution
  - EventSystem → events

- Avoid inheritance-heavy designs.
- Prefer plain classes and simple functions.

## Game Design Constraints (MVP)

- Grid-based movement only (no physics engine)
- Turn-based gameplay
- One player
- One enemy type initially
- No animations required
- No UI frameworks

## Code Constraints

- All logic must be readable and explicit
- No magic numbers — use constants
- Keep functions small
- Avoid async unless necessary

## Output Expectations

When generating code:
- Create complete files, not fragments
- Include imports
- Ensure code compiles
- Do not assume hidden context

## Anti-Goals (DO NOT DO)

- Do NOT implement:
  - inventory systems
  - save systems
  - complex AI
  - networking
  - animations beyond placeholders

- Do NOT refactor unrelated files

## Iteration Strategy

Always:
1. Implement the smallest working version
2. Verify it runs
3. Then extend

Never jump ahead.